IC_kwDOAEfiCM5co0dl","user":{"login":"CodePlayer","id":3793502,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3OTM1MDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3793502?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodePlayer","html_url":"https://github.com/CodePlayer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodePlayer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodePlayer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodePlayer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodePlayer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodePlayer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodePlayer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodePlayer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodePlayer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodePlayer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-05-19T08:08:22Z","updated_at":"2023-05-19T08:08:37Z","body":"> I see what you mean. The current solution is configured as forced remote in the settings, which should be able to solve it, or we can provide a rule to adapt to the requirements based on this broadcasting mechanism, and I will finish it later.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/PhoenixBackendon/dubbo/blob/35da167f6a921f9c0c0799b807442f72d0fefaff/dubbo-cluster/src/main/java/org/apache/dubbo/rpc/cluster/support/wrapper/ScopeClusterInvoker.java#L132\r\n`logger.debug()` should consider use placeholder `{}` .","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/dubbo/issues/comments/1554204517/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"CodePlayer","id":3793502,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3OTM1MDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3793502?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodePlayer","html_url":"https://github.com/CodePlayer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodePlayer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodePlayer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodePlayer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodePlayer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodePlayer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodePlayer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodePlayer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodePlayer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodePlayer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/dubbo/issues/comments/1554546614","html_url":"https://github.com/apache/dubbo/issues/12334#issuecomment-1554546614","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/dubbo/issues/12334","id":1554546614,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAEfiCM5cqH-2","user":{"login":"Phixsura","id":100568933,"node_id":"U_kgDOBf6PZQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/100568933?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Phixsura","html_url":"https://github.com/Phixsura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Phixsura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Phixsura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Phixsura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Phixsura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Phixsura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Phixsura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Phixsura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Phixsura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Phixsura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-05-19T13:07:45Z","updated_at":"2023-05-19T13:07:45Z","body":"> > I see what you mean. The current solution is configured as forced remote in the settings, which should be able to solve it, or we can provide a rule to adapt to the requirements based on this broadcasting mechanism, and I will finish it later.\r\n> \r\n> https://github.com/PhoenixBackendon/dubbo/blob/35da167f6a921f9c0c0799b807442f72d0fefaff/dubbo-cluster/src/main/java/org/apache/dubbo/rpc/cluster/support/wrapper/ScopeClusterInvoker.java#L132 `logger.debug()` should consider use placeholder `{}` .\r\n\r\n\r\nI completely agree with your point. Although the Dubbo logger is configuration-based and not all underlying loggers support placeholder-style value assignment, Dubbo currently only supports logger.debug(String message) instead of logger.debug(String message, Object... params) for logging. I suggest adding a conversion layer in the logger to enable placeholder-style logging, which would better align with elegant logging practices. This improvement would not only enhance code readability and maintainability but also provide greater flexibility and extensibility in logging. I propose that we create an issue to discuss and implement this enhancement.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/dubbo/issues/comments/1554546614/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"Phixsura","id":100568933,"node_id":"U_kgDOBf6PZQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/100568933?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Phixsura","html_url":"https://github.com/Phixsura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Phixsura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Phixsura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.githu